## 🗄️ Database Schema

### Tables

**1. `datasets`** — Uploaded dataset info
| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| id | INTEGER PK | Dataset ID |
| filename | TEXT | Original filename |
| filepath | TEXT | Storage path |
| rows | INTEGER | Row count |
| columns | INTEGER | Column count |
| uploaded_at | DATETIME | Upload timestamp |
| status | TEXT | pending / processing / done |

**2. `pipeline_runs`** — Pipeline execution record
| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| id | INTEGER PK | Run ID |
| dataset_id | INTEGER FK | Reference to dataset |
| started_at | DATETIME | Start time |
| completed_at | DATETIME | End time |
| overall_status | TEXT | running / success / failed |
| current_agent | TEXT | Active agent name |

**3. `agent_logs`** — Per-agent logs
| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| id | INTEGER PK | Log ID |
| run_id | INTEGER FK | Pipeline run reference |
| agent_name | TEXT | Agent identifier |
| status | TEXT | pending / running / done / failed |
| message | TEXT | Log message |
| duration_ms | INTEGER | Execution time |
| started_at | DATETIME | Start time |
| completed_at | DATETIME | End time |

**4. `quality_reports`** — Quality metrics
| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| id | INTEGER PK | Report ID |
| run_id | INTEGER FK | Pipeline run reference |
| total_rows | INTEGER | Total rows |
| null_count | INTEGER | Null cells |
| duplicate_count | INTEGER | Duplicate rows |
| outlier_count | INTEGER | Outliers detected |
| quality_score | FLOAT | 0–100 |
| details_json | TEXT | Detailed breakdown |

**5. `metadata_catalog`** — Column catalog
| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| id | INTEGER PK | Catalog entry ID |
| run_id | INTEGER FK | Pipeline run reference |
| column_name | TEXT | Column name |
| data_type | TEXT | Detected type |
| description | TEXT | AI-generated description |
| null_percent | FLOAT | % nulls |
| unique_count | INTEGER | Unique values |
| sample_values | TEXT | Sample data |

**6. `governance_reports`** — Compliance & PII
| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| id | INTEGER PK | Report ID |
| run_id | INTEGER FK | Pipeline run reference |
| pii_columns_json | TEXT | Detected PII columns |
| risk_level | TEXT | Low / Medium / High |
| compliance_status | TEXT | Pass / Fail |
| recommendations | TEXT | Action items |

---

## 🚀 Installation & Setup

### Prerequisites

- **Python** 3.11 or higher
- **Node.js** 18 or higher
- **npm** or **yarn**
- **Google Gemini API Key** → [Get it here](https://aistudio.google.com/apikey)
- **Git**

### 1️⃣ Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/vishakha2121/Multi-Agent-Autonomous-Enterprise-Data-Platform.git
cd Multi-Agent-Autonomous-Enterprise-Data-Platform
2️⃣ Backend Setup
bash
cd backend

# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate (Windows)
venv\Scripts\activate

# Activate (Mac/Linux)
source venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
3️⃣ Configure Environment Variables
Create backend/.env:

env
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./database/platform.db
UPLOAD_DIR=./uploads
OUTPUT_DIR=./outputs
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
4️⃣ Initialize Database
bash
python -c "from database import init_db; init_db()"
5️⃣ Run Backend Server
bash
uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000
Backend live at → http://localhost:8000
API Docs (Swagger) at → http://localhost:8000/docs

6️⃣ Frontend Setup
Open a new terminal:

bash
cd frontend
npm install
Create frontend/.env:

env
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
7️⃣ Run Frontend
bash
npm run dev
Frontend live at → http://localhost:5173

🔌 API Endpoints
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/upload	Upload a dataset (CSV/JSON/Excel)
POST	/api/pipeline/run	Trigger the 6-agent pipeline
GET	/api/pipeline/status/{run_id}	Get live pipeline status
GET	/api/pipeline/logs/{run_id}	Fetch agent logs
GET	/api/results/{run_id}	Fetch final output & reports
GET	/api/catalog	List metadata catalog entries
GET	/api/catalog/{run_id}	Catalog for a specific run
GET	/api/governance/report/{run_id}	PII & compliance report
GET	/api/dashboard/stats	Aggregated dashboard metrics
GET	/api/download/{run_id}	Download cleaned dataset
Full API documentation available at /docs (Swagger UI) once backend is running.

📸 Screenshots
(Add your screenshots here after building)

Page	Preview
Dashboard	docs/screenshots/dashboard.png
Upload	docs/screenshots/upload.png
Pipeline Flow	docs/screenshots/pipeline.png
Quality Report	docs/screenshots/quality.png
Metadata Catalog	docs/screenshots/catalog.png
Governance Report	docs/screenshots/governance.png
⚙️ How It Works
Step-by-step flow:

User uploads a file (CSV/JSON/Excel) via drag-and-drop UI

Ingestion Agent loads it into a DataFrame and registers the dataset

Validation Agent checks schema, required columns, data types

Quality Agent computes nulls, duplicates, outliers → quality score

Transformation Agent cleans the data (nulls, dups, formats, AI-suggested fixes)

Metadata Agent builds a catalog with AI-generated column descriptions

Governance Agent scans for PII, assigns risk levels, generates compliance report

Orchestrator logs every step → frontend shows real-time progress

User downloads the cleaned dataset + reports

All steps are logged in SQLite for full traceability.

🎯 Use Cases
🏢 Enterprise data onboarding — Automate first-pass cleaning & cataloging

🔐 GDPR / HIPAA compliance audits — PII detection & risk scoring

📚 Data cataloging — Auto-document datasets for analytics teams

🎓 Educational demos — Learn multi-agent system design

🧪 Prototyping — Rapid POC for autonomous data workflows

🔮 Future Scope
□ Add WebSocket for true real-time updates (currently polling)
□ Support database connectors (PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB)
□ Add scheduled pipelines (cron-based autonomy)
□ Implement agent-to-agent communication (message bus / RabbitMQ)
□ Add role-based access control (RBAC)
□ Multi-tenant support
□ Vector DB integration for semantic search on catalog
□ Migration to PostgreSQL for production
□ Docker & Kubernetes deployment
□ CI/CD pipeline with GitHub Actions
□ Fine-tune custom local LLM (when GPU available)
□ Anomaly detection using ML models
□ Slack / Email alerts on pipeline events
